<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>The Use of Large Language Models</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we employed GPT-5 to assist with the polishing of English text.
The model was used primarily for improving readability, clarity,
and fluency of the written content, ensuring that the final manuscript
meets high academic standards.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs and Derivations for EG-GRPO</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Detailed proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Per-batch budget balance). ‣ Budget view. ‣ 5.3 Entropy-Guided Token Selection ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (Per-batch budget balance)</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup and notation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For sequence <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{(i)}\!\triangleq\!|A^{(i)}|\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≜</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{(i)}\!\triangleq\!|A^{(i)}|\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(i)}\!\triangleq\!\mathrm{sign}(A^{(i)})\in\{\pm 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≜</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(i)}\!\triangleq\!\mathrm{sign}(A^{(i)})\in\{\pm 1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{(i)}_{t}\!\triangleq\!\bar{H}^{(i)}_{t}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≜</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{(i)}_{t}\!\triangleq\!\bar{H}^{(i)}_{t}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. With the low/mid/high partitions from Section <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Entropy-Guided Token Selection ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>, EG-GRPO’s per-sequence budget can be written as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}=(1-p_{\mathrm{lo}})\,a^{(i)}\;+\;\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\!\Big(\,\big|\,s^{(i)}a^{(i)}+\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}\,\big|-a^{(i)}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>EG</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>hi</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}=(1-p_{\mathrm{lo}})\,a^{(i)}\;+\;\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\!\Big(\,\big|\,s^{(i)}a^{(i)}+\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}\,\big|-a^{(i)}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Lemma 1 (Symmetric sign averaging).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\Big(|a+b|+|{-}a+b|\Big)=\max(a,b)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\Big(|a+b|+|{-}a+b|\Big)=\max(a,b).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof.</em> If <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq a</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a+b|=a+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a+b|=a+b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{-}a+b|=b-a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{-}a+b|=b-a</annotation></semantics></math>, so the average is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&lt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&lt;a</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a+b|=a+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a+b|=a+b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{-}a+b|=a-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{-}a+b|=a-b</annotation></semantics></math>, so the average is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Exact decomposition.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Taking expectation over <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> (assumed approximately symmetric due to group-normalization), Lemma 1 yields</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{s^{(i)}}\!\big[\,|s^{(i)}a^{(i)}+\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}|\,\big]=\max\!\big(a^{(i)},\,\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{s^{(i)}}\!\big[\,|s^{(i)}a^{(i)}+\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}|\,\big]=\max\!\big(a^{(i)},\,\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Plugging into equation <a href="#A2.E11" title="In Setup and notation. ‣ B.1 Detailed proof of Proposition (Per-batch budget balance) ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Derivations for EG-GRPO ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and using <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x-a)_{+}\!\triangleq\!\max(0,x-a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≜</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x-a)_{+}\!\triangleq\!\max(0,x-a)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{s^{(i)}}\!\big[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}\big]=(1-p_{\mathrm{lo}})\,a^{(i)}+\underbrace{\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\!\big(\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}-a^{(i)}\big)_{+}}_{\displaystyle\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>EG</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>hi</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.400em" minsize="1.400em">(</mo><mi mathsize="1.400em">i</mi><mo maxsize="1.400em" minsize="1.400em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{s^{(i)}}\!\big[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}\big]=(1-p_{\mathrm{lo}})\,a^{(i)}+\underbrace{\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\!\big(\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}-a^{(i)}\big)_{+}}_{\displaystyle\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Averaging over the batch <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}\!\big[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}\big]=(1-p_{\mathrm{lo}})\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[a^{(i)}]+\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}\!\big[\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>EG</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}\!\big[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}\big]=(1-p_{\mathrm{lo}})\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[a^{(i)}]+\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}\!\big[\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is nondecreasing in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and equals zero at <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Target equation for exact <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-scaling.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If one desires <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}]=\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[a^{(i)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>EG</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}]=\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[a^{(i)}]</annotation></semantics></math>, then equation <a href="#A2.E14" title="In Exact decomposition. ‣ B.1 Detailed proof of Proposition (Per-batch budget balance) ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Derivations for EG-GRPO ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> is equivalent to</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\!\big(\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}-a^{(i)}\big)_{+}=(\kappa-1+p_{\mathrm{lo}})\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}a^{(i)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>hi</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\!\big(\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}-a^{(i)}\big)_{+}=(\kappa-1+p_{\mathrm{lo}})\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}a^{(i)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The left-hand side is continuous, nondecreasing in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, hence admits a (numerically) unique solution for any <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Closed-form calibration (upper-bound match).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For an implementable closed form, use <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x-a)_{+}\leq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x-a)_{+}\leq x</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)\leq\lambda\cdot\underbrace{\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}h^{(i)}_{t}}_{\displaystyle H^{(i)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>hi</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi mathsize="1.400em">hi</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.400em" minsize="1.400em">(</mo><mi mathsize="1.400em">i</mi><mo maxsize="1.400em" minsize="1.400em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)\leq\lambda\cdot\underbrace{\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}h^{(i)}_{t}}_{\displaystyle H^{(i)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting this into equation <a href="#A2.E14" title="In Exact decomposition. ‣ B.1 Detailed proof of Proposition (Per-batch budget balance) ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Derivations for EG-GRPO ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> yields the upper bound</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}]\leq(1-p_{\mathrm{lo}})\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[a^{(i)}]+\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[H^{(i)}_{\mathrm{hi}}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>EG</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>lo</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>hi</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}]\leq(1-p_{\mathrm{lo}})\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[a^{(i)}]+\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[H^{(i)}_{\mathrm{hi}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Matching the <em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">upper bound</em> to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[a^{(i)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[a^{(i)}]</annotation></semantics></math> leads to the batch-calibrated choice</p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda^{\star}\;\triangleq\;\kappa\cdot\frac{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}a^{(i)}\cdot\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{lo}}}1}{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}h^{(i)}_{t}}\;=\;\kappa\cdot\frac{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}|A^{(i)}|\cdot\frac{|\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{lo}}|}{T^{(i)}}}{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\mathrm{sg}[\bar{H}^{(i)}_{t}]}\!," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>lo</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>hi</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>lo</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>hi</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda^{\star}\;\triangleq\;\kappa\cdot\frac{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}a^{(i)}\cdot\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{lo}}}1}{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}h^{(i)}_{t}}\;=\;\kappa\cdot\frac{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}|A^{(i)}|\cdot\frac{|\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{lo}}|}{T^{(i)}}}{\sum_{i\in\mathcal{B}}\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\mathrm{sg}[\bar{H}^{(i)}_{t}]}\!,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which is exactly equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In Proposition 1 (Per-batch budget balance). ‣ Budget view. ‣ 5.3 Entropy-Guided Token Selection ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. This calibration equates “saved” low-entropy budget with “reinvested” high-entropy mass in an upper-bound sense; see Remarks below.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks on calibration accuracy.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) Define the nonnegative discrepancy</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{(i)}(\lambda)\;\triangleq\;\lambda H^{(i)}_{\mathrm{hi}}-\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)=\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\min(\lambda h^{(i)}_{t},\,a^{(i)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>hi</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>hi</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{(i)}(\lambda)\;\triangleq\;\lambda H^{(i)}_{\mathrm{hi}}-\delta^{(i)}(\lambda)=\frac{1}{T^{(i)}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{S}^{(i,m)}_{\mathrm{hi}}}\min(\lambda h^{(i)}_{t},\,a^{(i)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It vanishes as <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}\!\gg\!a^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.108em">≫</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda h^{(i)}_{t}\!\gg\!a^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> for most high-entropy tokens, and is statistically damped by batch averaging. (ii) For <em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exact</em> <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-scaling, one may solve equation <a href="#A2.E15" title="In Target equation for exact 𝜅-scaling. ‣ B.1 Detailed proof of Proposition (Per-batch budget balance) ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Derivations for EG-GRPO ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> via a 1D root finder; we keep equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In Proposition 1 (Per-batch budget balance). ‣ Budget view. ‣ 5.3 Entropy-Guided Token Selection ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> for simplicity and stability. (iii) With <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=1</annotation></semantics></math>, equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In Proposition 1 (Per-batch budget balance). ‣ Budget view. ‣ 5.3 Entropy-Guided Token Selection ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> delivers batch-level budget neutrality in the calibrated upper-bound sense; empirically it closely tracks neutrality while avoiding per-step root solving.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conclusion.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining equation <a href="#A2.E14" title="In Exact decomposition. ‣ B.1 Detailed proof of Proposition (Per-batch budget balance) ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Derivations for EG-GRPO ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>–equation <a href="#A2.E16" title="In Closed-form calibration (upper-bound match). ‣ B.1 Detailed proof of Proposition (Per-batch budget balance) ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Derivations for EG-GRPO ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> with the calibration above yields
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}]\approx\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>EG</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>GRPO</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}]\approx\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}]</annotation></semantics></math>,
as stated in Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Per-batch budget balance). ‣ Budget view. ‣ 5.3 Entropy-Guided Token Selection ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Corollary 5.1 (Preserving GRPO stationary points). ‣ Fixed-point neutrality. ‣ 5.3 Entropy-Guided Token Selection ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> (Fixed-point neutrality)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(i)}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(i)}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in a batch. Then <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{(i)}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{(i)}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and the numerator of equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In Proposition 1 (Per-batch budget balance). ‣ Budget view. ‣ 5.3 Entropy-Guided Token Selection ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> vanishes, yielding <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. By equation <a href="#S5.E9" title="In 5.4 Entropy-Biased Advantage ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{A}^{(i)}_{t}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{A}^{(i)}_{t}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all tokens <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, so the loss equation <a href="#S5.E10" title="In 5.4 Entropy-Biased Advantage ‣ 5 Entropy-Guided Group Relative Policy Optimization ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> reduces to the reference-policy KL term. Hence any GRPO stationary point remains stationary under EG-GRPO, proving the corollary.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Optional exact per-batch scaling (implementation note)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If precise <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-scaling is required, solve the monotone equation equation <a href="#A2.E15" title="In Target equation for exact 𝜅-scaling. ‣ B.1 Detailed proof of Proposition (Per-batch budget balance) ‣ Appendix B Proofs and Derivations for EG-GRPO ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> for <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> by bisection or Newton’s method. This guarantees
<math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}]=\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>EG</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>GRPO</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{EG}}]=\kappa\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{B}}[B^{(i)}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}]</annotation></semantics></math>
<em id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exactly</em> per batch, at the cost of a 1D search.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Instruction for WISE</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="557.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 557.29" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,557.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#808080;" fill="#808080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 551.38 C 0 554.64 2.64 557.29 5.91 557.29 L 544.09 557.29 C 547.36 557.29 550 554.64 550 551.38 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 536.02 L 548.03 536.02 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 541.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">WISE Instruction</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:36.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="510.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 507.75)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are asked to write a concise text description to guide the generation of an image based on this prompt: “{}”.
Provide a brief, precise visualization of all elements in the prompt. Your description should:</span></span>
<span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Include every object mentioned.
<br class="ltx_break">2. Specify visual attributes (color, number, shape, texture) if given.
<br class="ltx_break">3. Clarify spatial or relational positioning if specified.
<br class="ltx_break">4. Be concise (<math id="A3.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq</annotation></semantics></math>50 words) but include the most common features and states inferred from real-world knowledge.
<br class="ltx_break">5. Apply real-world knowledge (cultural, religious, temporal, spatial, biological, physical, or chemical reasoning) and select only the single most relevant aspect that naturally enhances the original prompt to infer context (e.g., season, appearance, identity, cultural usage, or natural state) and reflect it in the objects. Use direct, widely accepted interpretations; include cultural or religious meanings only when they are common real-world associations. Avoid abstract or purely metaphorical interpretations.
<br class="ltx_break">6. Emphasize the current state of each object individually, as inferred from its environment or context. Reason separately for each object, considering temporal, cultural, or physical factors, and prioritize states logically implied by the prompt.
<br class="ltx_break">7. If multiple objects are present, reason from each object’s inherent physical or chemical properties and their interactions with the environment and with all other objects. Ensure that the inferred state, behavior, and interaction of every single object is logically correct and consistent with real-world rules, and clearly describe all differences and interactions relative to each other.
<br class="ltx_break">8. Ensure realism and aesthetic quality: all objects and interactions must follow real-world rules and appear visually consistent and appealing.
<br class="ltx_break">9. Do not omit objects explicitly mentioned, or add ones not specified or logically inferred.
<br class="ltx_break">10. Always preserve and emphasize the original objects and scene as the primary focus.
<br class="ltx_break">11. Always output a complete natural language description, never an image or symbolic shorthand.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>COMPUTATIONAL EFFICIENCY AND CONVERGENCE ANALYSIS</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To address concerns regarding the computational overhead of the proposed EG-GRPO, specifically the token-level entropy computation, percentile thresholding, and batch-level bonus recalibration, we conducted a rigorous benchmarking comparison of our method against the baseline T2I-R1.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>WALL-CLOCK TIME AND MEMORY OVERHEAD</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We measured the training step time and peak GPU memory usage on NVIDIA A100 GPUs under identical experimental settings. As shown in Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ D.1 WALL-CLOCK TIME AND MEMORY OVERHEAD ‣ Appendix D COMPUTATIONAL EFFICIENCY AND CONVERGENCE ANALYSIS ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, EG-GRPO introduces negligible overhead.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric</span></th>
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">T2I-R1 (Baseline)</span></th>
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EG-GRPO (Ours)</span></th>
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overhead</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Step Time (s)</th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">50.20</td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">50.88</td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">+1.35%</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">GPU Memory (GB)</th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">30.79</td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">31.17</td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">   +0.38 GB</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Computational overhead comparison between T2I-R1 and EG-GRPO. The overhead introduced by our entropy-guided mechanism is marginal in both time and memory.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The minimal increase in wall-clock time (<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 1.35\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>1.35</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 1.35\%</annotation></semantics></math>) suggests that the complexity of entropy operations (<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(L\cdot V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(L\cdot V)</annotation></semantics></math> for sequence length <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and vocabulary size <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>) is trivial compared to the computational cost of the model’s forward and backward passes. Importantly, this overhead ratio is expected to decrease further as model scale increases (e.g., larger hidden dimensions), as the entropy calculation depends only on the output logits and not the model depth or parameter count.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>CONVERGENCE EFFICIENCY</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While the per-step cost is marginally higher, EG-GRPO exhibits significantly better sample efficiency. We compared the reward progression of both models over the same number of training steps. As detailed in Table <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ D.2 CONVERGENCE EFFICIENCY ‣ Appendix D COMPUTATIONAL EFFICIENCY AND CONVERGENCE ANALYSIS ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, EG-GRPO consistently achieves higher rewards earlier in the training process.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">100</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">200</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">400</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">600</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">800</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Reward (T2I-R1)</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">2.1105</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">2.1130</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">2.1208</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">2.1339</td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">2.1340</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Reward (EG-GRPO)</th>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T6.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2.1411</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T6.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2.1836</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T6.2.3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2.1968</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T6.2.3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2.2075</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T6.2.3.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2.2117</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Convergence comparison: Reward scores at different training steps. EG-GRPO achieves higher performance consistently, indicating a superior time-to-convergence ratio.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This superior convergence efficiency outweighs the slight computational overhead, making EG-GRPO a more practical choice for large-scale training.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>QUALITATIVE DIVERSITY CASES</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To qualitatively compare the diversity of T2I-R1 and EG-GRPO, we generate 20 samples for each of three identical prompts and concatenate them for side-by-side visualization, as shown in Figure <a href="#A5.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix E QUALITATIVE DIVERSITY CASES ‣ From Broad Exploration to Stable Synthesis: Entropy-Guided Optimization for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. For a fair comparison, samples from both models are selected under comparable generation quality scores.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02355v1/all_prompts_montage.png" id="A5.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:439/634;" width="439" height="634" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Comparison of generation diversity for <span id="A5.F7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">T2I-R1</span> (left) and <span id="A5.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EG-GRPO</span> (right).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</article>
